@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: OpenCode keeps its own SQLite history inside the retained sbx engine; proveo imports it once into a new engine and carries it across a replacement
' covers: internal/sbx/opencode_history.go
' covers: internal/sbx/opencode_history_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_engine.go (landing)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_engine_test.go (landing)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt.go (retireSandbox: the D1 carry)
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_runtime.py
' covers: defs/opencode/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: internal/imagetest/opencode_test.go
'   the receipt and retire rules ...... _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml
'   native config, --auto, presentation _spec/defs/opencode/native-v2-integration.puml
'   the seed and the await ............ _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
'   the OAuth policy (still PLANNED) .. _spec/_paradigms/opencode-oauth-persistence.puml
'   the plan this replaces ............ _spec/_plans/opencode-versioned-history-storage.puml
'     (to be deleted once its source SPEC: pointers move here — D9)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── STATUS (2026-10-17) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' DECIDED by the user on 2026-10-16 (TUI; D1–D9 below). This spec is written
' FIRST, as the goal; the code lands in parallel — the host side from the
' coordinator, the image side from another agent (repo-simplification.puml D2,
' "(wt) in progress").
' MEASURED here: internal/sbx/opencode_history.go and its four tests
' (opencode_history_test.go: import installs a WAL database once and refuses a
' second; a corrupt copy is refused; the export streams a consistent copy;
' the argv targets the engine). EVERYTHING ELSE below that is not marked
' MEASURED is the coordinator's description of code still landing, and is
' [Unverified] here until it does.
'
' ── THE DECISIONS (the user, 2026-10-16; verbatim TUI labels where given) ───
' The architect's brief recommended an option for each; where the user chose
' differently, the user's answer is what this spec records.
'   D1 "Carry the DB over" — when an engine's settings change (the image after
'      `proveo build`, the kit, the mounts) and it is replaced, its database is
'      copied to the host and imported into the new engine. (The architect had
'      recommended never retiring without a headed yes; the user chose the
'      carry.)
'   D2 `--shell`: "if `proveo` retire it" — retired 2026-10-17. A shell in the
'      engine is sbx's: `sbx exec -it <engine> bash`.
'   D3 keep injecting `--standalone` (and `--auto` for headless `run`).
'   D4 "Let OpenCode handle it" — no proveo lock on concurrent launches.
'   D5 an import failure removes the fresh engine and its receipt, stops the
'      run, and the next run retries.
'   D6 every new engine imports once.
'   D7 engines created before this change retire like any sandbox; their
'      history sits in the V2 share and the import restores it; the legacy
'      owner record is deleted.
'   D8 "Accept and document" — in-engine logins persist until `sbx rm`.
'   D9 this spec, then delete _spec/_plans/opencode-versioned-history-storage.puml
'      after rehoming the facts that still matter (REHOMED below).
'
' ── WHERE THE DATABASE LIVES ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' OpenCode's native default: $HOME/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db, with HOME
' = /home/agent in sbx. proveo sets neither OPENCODE_DB nor XDG_DATA_HOME for an
' agent launch. The engine scripts resolve the path the way OpenCode does
' (MEASURED, opencode_history.go openCodeDatabasePath): OPENCODE_DB, else
' $XDG_DATA_HOME/opencode/opencode.db, else ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db.
' The file is on the engine's own disk. It survives reattach and `sbx stop`
' and goes with `sbx rm` (REHOMED, sbx persistence). proveo never writes it
' back to the host: the two entrypoint-lib.sh sync skips that keep
' .local/share/opencode off the host stay.
'
' ── A NEW ENGINE IMPORTS ONCE (ensureOpenCodeEngine; D6) ───────────────────
'   1. `sbx create`, not `sbx run`: the import must finish before the agent's
'      first open, and `sbx run` starts the agent at once.
'   2. The source is the FIRST REGULAR FILE (symlinks rejected) of, under the
'      proveo home:
'        opencode/carry/<engine>.db         (the D1 carry)
'        opencode/v2/share/opencode.db      (the V2 share)
'        opencode/share/opencode.db         (the pre-V2 share)
'        .local/share/opencode/opencode.db
'      [Unverified] With none of them the engine starts empty.
'   3. The host `sbx cp`s the db plus any -wal and -journal to
'      /tmp/proveo-import-opencode.db* (MEASURED: OpenCodeImportCopyArgs,
'      OpenCodeImportStage). It stats the source before and after and aborts
'      if it changed; it never copies -shm and never writes the source.
'   4. `sbx exec -w / <engine> -- python3 -I -c OpenCodeImportScript <stage>`
'      (MEASURED, OpenCodeImportArgs / OpenCodeImportScript): exit 3 at once if
'      the engine already has a database; else copy the stage into a private
'      temp dir, `PRAGMA quick_check` (exit 4 on failure), fold the WAL through
'      SQLite's backup API into a temp file BESIDE the target, chmod 0600,
'      `link()` it into place — never over an existing file — and remove the
'      stage (-shm included) on every path. Exit 0 = imported.
'   5. `sbx run --name <engine>` reattaches and the agent starts.
'   6. A consumed carry file is deleted after a successful import. The host V2
'      share is NEVER edited.
' D5: on ANY import failure the fresh engine is `sbx rm`'d and its receipt
' removed, and the run stops; the carry file stays, so the next run retries.
'
' ── A REPLACED ENGINE CARRIES ITS DATABASE (D1, D7) ────────────────────────
' retireSandbox, for an OpenCode engine, first runs `sbx exec -w / <engine> --
' python3 -I -c OpenCodeExportScript` (MEASURED: OpenCodeExportArgs /
' OpenCodeExportScript). It opens the engine database with a 30 s busy timeout,
' takes a backup-API single-file copy, switches the copy to DELETE journal mode
' and streams it on stdout; exit 3 (OpenCodeExportNone) when the engine has no
' database. The host writes <home>/opencode/carry/<engine>.db.partial, checks
' the SQLite header (OpenCodeDatabaseHeader, MEASURED), and renames it to .db
' with mode 0600.
'   exit 3 → a legacy keeper engine (D7: its history lived in a /tmp cache,
'     not at the native path) → nothing carried; the next import falls back to
'     the V2 share. retireSandbox deletes the legacy owner record.
'   any other export failure → retire refuses and the old engine is kept.
' The opencode-only "engine is running" refusal in retireIfStale is gone:
' OpenCode follows the generic stale-sandbox rule (kit-lifecycle.puml), and the
' headed upgrade prompt gains a line saying the history is carried over.
'
' ── RETENTION AND REMOVAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A normal end keeps the engine (normalEndOf → endRetainEngine) and prints
' "OpenCode: history lives in retained engine <name>" — e2e/seed_ready_test.go
' matches the substring "retained engine ". `sbx rm` deletes the engine and
' its history, and so does the Ctrl+C "remove" answer; no carry runs on either.
'
' ── THE IMAGE SIDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' defs/opencode/harness.manifest loses the opencode/v2/share mount
' (MEASURED today: still present at lines 24-25, mapped to
' /proveo-home/.local/share/opencode); opencode/v2/config stays.
' packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime becomes a THIN WRAPPER, keeping its name
' so the image shim stays: it injects `--auto` (headless `run`) and
' `--standalone` (D3); diagnostics and the git-sync commit-subject helper run
' unchanged in a throwaway data, state and DB dir with OpenCode's service
' disabled; everything else is a plain execv of the native client. No
' supervise, leases, credential helper, version check, preflight, journal or
' cache.
' DELETED with this change: packages/lib/opencode_cache.py,
' opencode-credentials.py, proveo-opencode-preflight, opencode_startup.py,
' opencode-runtime-fixture.py; internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_cache.go and
' its tests; internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_history_image_test.go; the
' prepared-history seed gate (proveo-seed, defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh); the
' keeper parts of proveo-await-seed; and the reset/prepare/recovery prompts in
' internal/choiceui. The load_credentials()/Keeper env split recorded in the old
' plan's TEST DELETIONS goes with load_credentials itself.
'
' ── REHOMED FROM THE DELETED PLAN (D9) ─────────────────────────────────────
' SBX PERSISTENCE AND REMOVAL (docs read 2026-10-14, quoted then):
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/architecture/ : everything inside a
'     sandbox "persists until you remove it", "agent state and history"
'     included; `sbx rm` deletes "all of its contents".
'   https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/releases v0.42.0: a new sandbox
'     reusing a deleted name "no longer inherits its files, Docker images, or
'     agent session history".
'   "By default, a local sandbox stops automatically shortly after its last
'     session disconnects" (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/
'     author/; 30 s grace, docker/sbx-releases#452; `sbx create` sandboxes since
'     v0.43.0). "The rest of the VM filesystem persists across restarts"
'     (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/isolation/); processes
'     and memory do not. That auto-stop is what killed the old in-memory
'     keeper ~30 s after every run; an on-disk database is unaffected.
' KIT LIMITS (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits-v2/, read
' 2026-10-14): startup commands "don't gate the agent's entrypoint"; "Use
' setup.files for any value that needs to land on disk before the agent runs";
' setup.files writes text content; a kit "can't read arbitrary host environment
' variables or files"; v2 volumes take no host source. So no kit surface can
' carry a SQLite database in — hence `sbx create` + `sbx cp` + `sbx exec` before
' the reattach. https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/agents/opencode/
' documents no data or history path and no import.
' SQLITE WAL ACROSS MACHINES:
'   * SQLite's active state stays on the ENGINE'S LOCAL filesystem, never a
'     database shared across VMs through a mount: WAL coordinates writers
'     through the -shm shared-memory index, which only works between
'     processes on one host ([Unverified] https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html).
'     Cross-VM file locking through sbx mounts was never measured.
'   * Every OpenCode 2.x database runs in WAL mode; a clean exit removes -wal
'     and -shm, and OpenCode writes the database on every open.
'   * SQLite cannot open a WAL database read-only in a directory where it
'     cannot create the -shm (measured 2026-10-15: "unable to open database
'     file"; [Unverified] https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html, "Read-Only
'     Databases"). So the import never opens the stage where it lands: it
'     copies it into a private writable temp dir first, and it never copies a
'     -shm, which describes another machine's memory.
' E2E FACTS: an sbx e2e must keep the operator's HOME, where sbx keeps its
' login — with a temporary HOME `sbx template load` failed "Not authenticated
' to Docker" (2026-10-15); only PROVEO_HOME is temporary. [Inference] `sbx run`
' with no TTY and stdin at EOF does not return the agent's output, so e2e legs
' drive proveo on a pty. Each "[A]pprove all" saves a per-service binding in
' the operator's ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, which outlives the test.
'
' ── RISKS, RECORDED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   * D8: credentials live with the engine. V2 keeps tokens in SQLite beside
'     the sessions; an in-engine login now persists until `sbx rm`, readable
'     by the agent's uid and by `sbx exec`, and proveo never moves it to the
'     host. [Unverified] A legacy V1 database may carry credential rows into
'     the import.
'   * `sbx rm` loses the history unless a carry ran first: the Ctrl+C remove,
'     an operator's `sbx rm`, and name reuse all lose it.
'   * Every engine in every workspace imports the same snapshot of the share,
'     and the copies diverge; nothing merges them back.
'   * [Unverified] `sbx cp` file ownership in the engine — the import copies
'     the stage into its own temp dir before opening it, so a root-owned stage
'     is read, not written.
'   * [Unverified] OpenCode's behaviour with two clients on one SQLite
'     database (D4: no proveo lock; the old runtime refused a second client
'     with exit 75).
'   * The first launch on a new engine pays the copy (measured store sizes:
'     _spec/packages/lib/opencode-seed-progress.puml) plus OpenCode's own
'     migration; later launches do no proveo history work.
'   * The git-sync commit-subject helper runs on a throwaway database, so it
'     cannot use an in-engine OAuth login ([Inference]; it falls back to the
'     paths summary, _spec/packages/lib/git-sync-turn.puml).
'
' ── NON-GOALS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' No host-side store, publication, sanitizer, cross-engine sharing or merge.
' No backup or export command. No docker-backend path. No host-owned OAuth (it
' stays PLANNED). The host V2 share is never deleted or edited. Other
' harnesses retire as before.
title OpenCode engine-local history — import once, carry on replacement, keep until sbx rm

participant "proveo run opencode\n(host)" as PV <<app>>
database "proveo home\nopencode/carry · v2/share · share" as HOMEDB <<db>>
participant "sbx" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "engine\n~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db" as ENG <<host>>
participant "opencode\nthin runtime → native" as OC <<app>>

group new engine (ensureOpenCodeEngine)
  PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx create <engine>
  PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : first regular file:\ncarry/<engine>.db · v2/share · share · .local/share
  PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx cp db (+ -wal, -journal) → stage\nsource stat before/after; never -shm
  PV ARROW_MAIN ENG : sbx exec python3 -I -c OpenCodeImportScript
  ENG ARROW_MAIN ENG : private copy · quick_check · backup API\nlink() only if absent · 0600
  alt exit 0
    PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : delete the consumed carry file
  else any failure (D5)
    PV ARROW_ERROR SBX : sbx rm <engine>; receipt removed; run stops
  end
end
PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx run --name <engine> (reattach)
SBX ARROW_MAIN OC : agent launch
OC ARROW_MAIN ENG : native default path; --auto / --standalone
PV ARROW_OPTIONAL PV : teardown keeps the engine:\n"history lives in retained engine <name>"

group settings changed (retireSandbox, D1 / D7)
  PV ARROW_MAIN ENG : sbx exec python3 -I -c OpenCodeExportScript
  ENG ARROW_MAIN PV : stdout: single-file copy (DELETE journal)
  PV ARROW_MAIN HOMEDB : carry/<engine>.db.partial → header check → .db (0600)
  alt exit 3: legacy keeper engine (D7)
    PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : nothing carried; the V2 share is the source
  else export failed
    PV ARROW_ERROR PV : retire refuses; the old engine is kept
  end
  PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx rm --force <engine>, then a new engine (above)
end

note over ENG
  **The engine owns the database.** proveo
  sets no OPENCODE_DB or XDG_DATA_HOME, so
  OpenCode opens its own default path, kept
  until ""sbx rm"".
end note

note right of PV
  **Import once, read-only.** The host copies
  the source and checks it did not change; it
  never copies -shm and never writes it.
end note

note over SBX
  **A failed import removes the new engine.**
  Its receipt goes too, the carry file stays,
  and the next run tries again.
end note

note right of HOMEDB
  **A replaced engine carries its database.**
  The export lands in opencode/carry, and the
  next new engine imports it first.
end note

note over OC
  **The runtime only shapes argv.** It adds
  --auto and --standalone, then execs the
  native client.
end note
@enduml
